  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` has front matter, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions`. Its `description` states when to use the skill in terms of the user's task. It covers design sessions and changes to code, tests or requirement text, including when the user only asks for a feature, bug fix, CLI flag, test, dependency bump or wording tweak. It also covers writing or revising reference chapters. It names `habeas-refactor` and `habeas-evidence` only as alternatives where an agent could confuse them, which the requirement allows with MAY. No obligation is unmet, and there are no violation matches to judge.",
